                        <field name="dc_date">1080-1096 </field>
                        <field name="dc_description">This is a meticulous copy of Augustine’s De trinitate, written in a single-column; it has an opening page and a page with a decorative initial, as well as several initials with scroll ornamentation of varying heights at the beginning of each book. The manuscript is listed in the All Saints Abbey register of books from about 1100 (Min. 17, f. 306v). In the 15th century this codex, like many others, received a new leather binding with metal bosses and two clasps; as with Min. 24‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬ and Min. 40‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬, fragments from a 14th century necrology of All Saints Abbey were used as pastedowns and flyleaves. </field>
